    "turn_text": "I think that, here's what bothered me more. There are a lot of things that bothered me on all sides, and there were a lot of things that said that, are true and there are a lot of things that I'm worried about, but there was no, normally that's a time we come together. You know, it's one of the few times that you have all three branches of government, congressional, the legislative, the executive, and the Supreme Court. There was no uniting moment. There was no, everybody, you know, what, where do we have something in common? And I, honestly, that is part of what the person giving speech should try to do. I think that Democrats are trying to figure out how to react to the moment. The fact of the matter is Republicans have the majority. They have the majority in the Senate, the House, and the White House. There are things that are happening that people are angry about and they want to see Democrats do something about. And you, different people do different things. Leadership ask members. to please not use props. I was there when they were bearing intense conversation. But everybody's an individual. You know, Marjorie Taylor Greene wore her mega hat and broke the house. I mean, everybody, you know, you got. You can't control members.",
